# LAB 1 – Temperature Sensor with Relay Control (Telegram)

## Overview

This project uses an ESP32 with a DHT22 temperature and humidity sensor together with a relay module. The ESP32 reads temperature and humidity data every 5 seconds and sends alerts through Telegram when the temperature rises above a threshold value.

Users can control the relay remotely using Telegram commands such as `/status`, `/on`, and `/off`. When the temperature drops below the threshold again, the relay automatically turns OFF.

This project was developed using MicroPython in Thonny IDE.

