# Wiring Diagram

| Component  | ESP32 Pin |
| ---------- | --------- |
| DHT22 DATA | GPIO16    |
| Relay IN   | GPIO25    |
| DHT22 VCC  | 5V        |
| Relay VCC  | 5V        |
| GND        | GND       |



# Task 1 – Sensor Read & Print

The ESP32 reads temperature and humidity data from the DHT22 sensor every 5 seconds and prints the values to the serial monitor.

## Features

* Reads temperature
* Reads humidity
* Updates every 5 seconds
* Handles sensor read errors



# Task 2 – Telegram Send

The ESP32 connects to Telegram using the Telegram Bot API and sends messages to the Telegram group.

## Features

* Connects ESP32 to WiFi
* Connects to Telegram Bot
* Receives Telegram updates
* Sends test messages



# Task 3 – Telegram Commands

The Telegram bot supports remote commands for controlling the relay and checking sensor status.

## Commands

### `/status`

Shows:

* Temperature
* Humidity
* Relay state

### `/on`

Turns relay ON.

### `/off`

Turns relay OFF.

## Example


Temp: 34.00 C
Humidity: 70.00 %
Light: ON


---

# Task 4 – Alert Logic & Auto OFF

The ESP32 automatically monitors temperature levels and sends Telegram warning messages when the temperature exceeds the threshold.

## Alert Logic

* No alerts are sent when temperature is below the threshold
* If temperature exceeds the threshold:

  * Telegram sends warning messages every 5 seconds
* User sends `/on` to activate relay
* Alerts stop after relay is ON
* When temperature drops below threshold:

  * Relay automatically turns OFF
  * Telegram sends an auto-OFF message

## Example Alert


ALERT: Temp is 35.00 C
Above threshold!
Send /on to turn light ON.
```

## Example Auto OFF Message


Temp dropped below threshold.
Light auto-OFF.

